[38;2;124;124;124mThis is the Pontryagin duality question. The answer is yes — compact metrizable [0m[38;2;124;124;124mabelian groups have enough characters to separate points. This is a consequence [0m[38;2;124;124;124mof Pontryagin duality / the Peter-Weyl theorem for compact groups (which applies[0m[38;2;124;124;124mto compact abelian groups as a special case).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me construct a proof.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mApproach 1: Use Pontryagin duality. For a locally compact abelian group $G$, the[0m[38;2;124;124;124mnatural map $G \to \widehat{\widehat{G}}$ is an isomorphism of topological [0m
